    {
      "id": "mU0w6FRpi_tjG0P8Mknz5",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 249,
      "y": 703,
      "width": 862.679443359375,
      "height": 1025,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aT",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1879054600,
      "version": 968,
      "versionNonce": 205414431,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1763841168931,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "With spring\n\nwe don't use (new keyword)\n\nA bean is an object that Spring creates, stores, and manages for you.\n\nWhy are beans needed?\nSo that:\nyou don’t need to manually create objects\nyou don’t use new everywhere\nSpring can automatically connect objects to each other (Dependency Injection)\nyou get cleaner code\neasier testing\ncentralized configuration\n\n\nwe define a bean using annotations.\n\nBy putting special annotations on a class\n\n\n\nSpring sees the annotation → Spring creates the object → that object becomes a bean.\n\n\n@Component\npublic class MyService { }\n\n@Service                                                          All of these create beans.\npublic class UserService { }                                     \n\n\n@Repository\npublic class UserRepository { }\n                                                          \n\n@RestController\npublic class UserController { }\n\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "With spring\n\nwe don't use (new keyword)\n\nA bean is an object that Spring creates, stores, and manages for you.\n\nWhy are beans needed?\nSo that:\nyou don’t need to manually create objects\nyou don’t use new everywhere\nSpring can automatically connect objects to each other (Dependency Injection)\nyou get cleaner code\neasier testing\ncentralized configuration\n\n\nwe define a bean using annotations.\n\nBy putting special annotations on a class\n\n\n\nSpring sees the annotation → Spring creates the object → that object becomes a bean.\n\n\n@Component\npublic class MyService { }\n\n@Service                                                          All of these create beans.\npublic class UserService { }                                     \n\n\n@Repository\npublic class UserRepository { }\n                                                          \n\n@RestController\npublic class UserController { }\n\n\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
