      "text": "@PreDestroy\n\nWhen does it run?\n\nIt runs just before the bean is destroyed, usually when:\nSpring application context closes\nApplication is shutting down",
      "fontSize": 12.11428571428571,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "@PreDestroy\n\nWhen does it run?\n\nIt runs just before the bean is destroyed, usually when:\nSpring application context closes\nApplication is shutting down",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "wtQskULnaQGG8DTyhdGRv",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 157,
      "y": 1852,
      "width": 768.0394287109375,
      "height": 1475,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0C",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2016724177,
      "version": 128,
      "versionNonce": 502504049,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1763842358780,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Bean Scope\n\nBean scope means how long a bean lives in the \nSpring container AND how Spring returns that bean when requested.\n\n\nSingleton (default)\nOnly one instance of the bean is created for the entire Spring application.\nSame object returned every time.\n\n@Component\npublic class PaymentService {}\n\nThis is a singleton bean by default.\n\n System.out.println(paymentObj1.hashCode());\n System.out.println(paymentObj2.hashCode());\n\n\n        paymentObj1.pay();\n        paymentObj2.pay();\n\n898283008                             Output\n898283008\nPaying....\nPaying....\n\n\n\n\nPrototype\n\nEvery time you ask the bean, Spring creates a new object.\nUseful when you need separate stateful objects.\n\n\n\n@Scope(\"prototype\")\n@Component\npublic class PaymentService {}\n\nImportant:   Prototype beans are NOT managed fully by Spring after creation.\n@PreDestroy will NOT run for prototype scope.\n\n\n\nSystem.out.println(paymentObj1.hashCode());\nSystem.out.println(paymentObj2.hashCode());\n\n\n        paymentObj1.pay();\n        paymentObj2.pay();\n\n\n1973471376\n898283008\nPaying....\nPaying....\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Bean Scope\n\nBean scope means how long a bean lives in the \nSpring container AND how Spring returns that bean when requested.\n\n\nSingleton (default)\nOnly one instance of the bean is created for the entire Spring application.\nSame object returned every time.\n\n@Component\npublic class PaymentService {}\n\nThis is a singleton bean by default.\n\n System.out.println(paymentObj1.hashCode());\n System.out.println(paymentObj2.hashCode());\n\n\n        paymentObj1.pay();\n        paymentObj2.pay();\n\n898283008                             Output\n898283008\nPaying....\nPaying....\n\n\n\n\nPrototype\n\nEvery time you ask the bean, Spring creates a new object.\nUseful when you need separate stateful objects.\n\n\n\n@Scope(\"prototype\")\n@Component\npublic class PaymentService {}\n\nImportant:   Prototype beans are NOT managed fully by Spring after creation.\n@PreDestroy will NOT run for prototype scope.\n\n\n\nSystem.out.println(paymentObj1.hashCode());\nSystem.out.println(paymentObj2.hashCode());\n\n\n        paymentObj1.pay();\n        paymentObj2.pay();\n\n\n1973471376\n898283008\nPaying....\nPaying....\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
